Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.74,0:01:36.23,Flashback,Mushroom Lord,0,0,0,,Well.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.99,0:01:39.62,Flashback,Mushroom Lord,0,0,0,,Hello, Luna.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.07,0:01:41.53,Flashback,Luna,0,0,0,,Master.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.53,0:01:47.80,Flashback,Mushroom Lord,0,0,0,,So you have finally encountered the one \Ndestined to become The End to All Things,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.80,0:01:49.71,Flashback,Mushroom Lord,0,0,0,,the cursed youngling.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.06,0:01:51.38,Flashback,Luna,0,0,0,,The cursed youngling!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.30,0:01:57.25,Flashback,Mushroom Lord,0,0,0,,Step closer, Luna. Leave all of \Nyour overflowing poison with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.02,0:02:04.69,Flashback,Mushroom Lord,0,0,0,,Even for you, the poison from The End \Nof All Things is too heavy to bear.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.85,0:02:11.41,Flashback,Luna,0,0,0,,The boy was very beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.83,0:02:17.05,Flashback_Italics,Luna (M),0,0,0,,I could sense it in the \Nmushroom I drew from him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.85,0:02:19.98,Flashback_Italics,Luna (M),0,0,0,,It was as if his soul was crystal clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.08,0:02:27.07,Flashback,Mushroom Lord,0,0,0,,And that may be exactly what makes \Nhim turn in to The End of All Things.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.68,0:02:31.75,Flashback,Mushroom Lord,0,0,0,,And Luna,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.98,0:02:35.97,Flashback,Mushroom Lord,0,0,0,,as he is, so are you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.26,0:02:39.48,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,What was that?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.82,0:02:43.24,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,EPISODE 4: THE BLACK WITCH COUNCIL
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.97,0:02:42.45,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,Luna used to be a cursed \Nyoungling herself?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.97,0:02:50.54,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,So just like this brat, Luna was destined \Nto turn into The End of All Things.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.35,0:02:55.65,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,But if Luna {\i0}used{\i1} to be one, that means...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.32,0:03:00.38,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Black magicians are forced to combat \Ncontamination, hatred, and plague
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.38,0:03:04.11,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,as they work to eradicate\N the various poisons of this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.57,0:03:07.48,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,So unlike humans or even normal magicians,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.95,0:03:09.99,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,they have a strong tolerance to poison.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.21,0:03:20.13,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Many of them keep poisonous \Ncreatures as familiars
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.13,0:03:22.25,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,to assist in their purification efforts.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.34,0:03:29.48,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,As such, people tend to lump us magicians \Ntogether as "poison magicians,"
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.48,0:03:33.86,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,but the truth is that we merely have \Na stronger tolerance to poison than most.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.05,0:03:41.96,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Luna, however, with her poison breath \Nand skin, along with her ability to absorb
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.49,0:03:46.09,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,poisons into her body, has a power \Nthat even poisonous creatures don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.09,0:03:50.11,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,There is only one magician whose body can \Nbreak down and purify poisons like that
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.96,0:03:55.61,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,in this entire world, and that is Luna.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.45,0:04:01.59,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,And she was once the \Ncursed youngling herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.55,0:04:06.60,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Seeing as she was once destined \Nto become The End of All Things,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.60,0:04:08.74,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,her ability is likely \Na remnant of that past.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.86,0:04:11.60,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Wow.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.86,0:04:11.60,Default - Top,Merino,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.60,0:04:15.50,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,A remnant of her destiny to \Nbecome The End of All Things?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.52,0:04:20.81,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,Does that mean even though \NLuna was the cursed youngling,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.81,0:04:23.03,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,she avoided turning into The End somehow?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.99,0:04:27.14,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.47,0:04:33.07,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,Anyway, that explains why \Nshe's protecting this kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.83,0:04:39.34,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,As far as we know, she is the only one
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.78,0:04:42.60,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,who's been able to escape that fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.84,0:04:48.09,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,So now they're the only two people in \Nthe world to have shared that curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.79,0:04:54.36,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,While Luna was the cursed youngling,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.36,0:04:57.35,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,she was also in possession \Nof great magical talent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.57,0:05:01.36,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,Without instruction from anyone,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.36,0:05:07.73,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,she was able to absorb all kinds of magic \Nfrom the land and air into her body.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.83,0:05:13.87,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,As she learned magic and her body \Ndeveloped the ability to clear poisons,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.25,0:05:16.92,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,she also passed every test we gave her
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.92,0:05:19.88,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,and overcame her fate \Nas a cursed youngling.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.14,0:05:39.65,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,There had never been anyone like her. \NShe was a uniquely impressive girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.65,0:05:42.62,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,Luna overcame her fate?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.40,0:05:49.30,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,We've wasted too much time \Nexplaining things to the crow.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.91,0:05:55.66,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Basically, her obvious talents convinced \Nus to let her live and take a gamble on
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.66,0:05:57.95,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,her potential as a poison magician.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.97,0:06:00.30,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.08,0:06:02.78,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,that boy is different.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.64,0:06:06.20,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,It will be too late once \Nhe turns into The End.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.17,0:06:11.72,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,If we don't kill the seed before it \Nsprouts and the curse awakens,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.72,0:06:15.85,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,many lives will be lost as the spread \Nof poison in the world accelerates.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.43,0:06:18.34,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Step away from that creature!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.19,0:06:20.44,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Flame.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.44,0:06:22.44,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,Hey. We're indoors.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.69,0:06:27.69,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,What is that thing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.83,0:06:36.08,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Luna!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.34,0:06:38.33,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Luna!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.65,0:06:39.75,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,Wh-Wha...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.21,0:06:41.33,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,Water?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.33,0:06:44.34,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,Wow. That's some nasty-looking \Ngrilled mushroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.34,0:06:47.08,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,He's always overcooking things.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.47,0:06:49.34,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.97,0:06:52.86,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,One moment, Claude.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.26,0:07:04.17,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,A hole?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.39,0:07:36.59,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,What the hell were you thinking?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.59,0:07:39.84,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,One wrong step and you would've \Nbeen burnt to a crisp!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.84,0:07:42.47,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Are you trying to get yourself \Nkilled for that brat?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.47,0:07:45.11,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,For once in your life, \Nwould you listen to people?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.11,0:07:48.01,Default - Top,Claude,0,0,0,,You got off easy this \Ntime, but I swear...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.11,0:07:50.27,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Bird. Why is he yelling at her \Nas if we weren't here?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.27,0:07:54.16,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Who knows? Maybe he just \Nreally hates pranks.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.16,0:07:55.16,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,Pfft.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.53,0:07:56.60,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,Oh, golly.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.41,0:07:59.16,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,Huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.09,0:08:02.82,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,What is it you find so humorous?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.17,0:08:13.43,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,It's a murder mushroom! Luna, when \Ndid you make that thing sprout? Wow!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.71,0:08:22.46,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Whoa, it's growing so big! \NSo much rage but not much-room!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.07,0:08:33.00,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Whoa! The murder mushroom burst \Nthrough the roof like fireworks!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.58,0:08:44.42,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,Man, a projection can \Ncause that much ruin?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.33,0:08:46.46,Italics,Claude (M),0,0,0,,Freaky.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.83,0:08:49.84,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Flame, control yourself in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.84,0:08:55.59,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,At any rate, in lieu of making rash \Ndecisions, let's all talk this through.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.59,0:08:58.78,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,We'd rather not have you sprouting \Nanother murder mushroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.10,0:09:04.60,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,We should also allow her\N to speak her piece.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.93,0:09:11.86,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I can feel a kernel of magic inside him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.17,0:09:13.86,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,What does that tell us?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.86,0:09:19.42,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,Only about as much as your average white \Nwitch. Not enough to make a difference.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.71,0:09:25.59,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Still, there's a chance it may be enough \Nto help him escape The End of All Things.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.12,0:09:28.30,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,Now we're just going around in circles.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.30,0:09:31.86,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,You can't cling to a fantasy just \Nbecause you lack the backbone
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.86,0:09:33.74,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,to take one meager life.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.77,0:09:38.14,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I will raise this child by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.27,0:09:43.85,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I know that I can make \Nhim into a magician.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.11,0:09:48.30,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I will pour everything I have into him,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.07,0:09:53.49,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,and make him a strong enough magician \Nto escape his fate as a cursed youngling.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.85,0:09:54.90,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I will...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.40,0:09:58.55,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I will!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.91,0:10:04.05,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I'm even starting to wonder
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.26,0:10:13.81,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,if I was allowed to defy my fate, if I'm\N still alive today, to fulfill this role.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.42,0:10:21.45,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I'm beginning to see our meeting \Nas a guidepost of destiny
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.97,0:10:24.77,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,showing me my future \Npath as a black witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.00,0:10:31.74,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,So you would raise the cursed \Nyoungling as a person
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.74,0:10:33.49,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,to prevent him from becoming The End.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.49,0:10:36.26,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Are you certain you can show him the way?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.73,0:10:41.59,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,With your only method being to \Nabsorb that poison into your body?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.35,0:10:46.46,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,When you aren't even a fully-fledged \Nblack witch yet? How, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.17,0:10:50.55,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,Plus you've never taken\N an apprentice before,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.96,0:10:52.67,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,and you're such a loner.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.96,0:10:55.96,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,You cling to fantasy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.21,0:11:02.44,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,And yet, I feel we can agree that it \Nis not particularly judicious to assume
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.44,0:11:07.18,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,that ending his life is the only option \Nwe have to stop The End of All Things
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.18,0:11:09.78,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,and protect the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.14,0:11:12.79,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Bird Magician...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.69,0:11:15.73,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,You say she clings to fantasy,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.98,0:11:23.37,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,but her life journey thus far has \Nbeen entirely unconventional.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.37,0:11:25.90,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,Perhaps even fantastical.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.25,0:11:32.23,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,Indeed, killing him off \Nand calling it all settled
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.23,0:11:34.49,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,would feel like somewhat \Nof an easy way out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.49,0:11:35.27,Default,Insect Magician,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.97,0:11:37.73,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Beast Magician...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.26,0:11:43.10,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,One could even say we're using \N"the future" as an excuse
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.10,0:11:44.76,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,to skirt risk and cut corners.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.78,0:11:45.90,Default,Insect Magician,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.51,0:11:53.06,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,We won't settle anything like this. Let's \Nput it to a formal vote as a council.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.75,0:11:56.07,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,The matter before us is,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.07,0:12:00.89,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,do we entrust Luna with the task of \Nthis boy's magic training or not?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.53,0:12:07.53,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Even if the majority vote is affirmative, \Nif there is any indication of the boy
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.53,0:12:11.04,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,failing at his studies, \Nhe will be put to death.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.27,0:12:15.22,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,If the majority vote is negative, \Nhe will be put to death immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.22,0:12:17.87,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,And the Champignon Witch will \Nbe sanctioned for disobedience.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.80,0:12:21.16,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,We will come back to that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.16,0:12:23.78,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Is that fair, Luna? Everyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.74,0:12:33.27,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Is that fair, Luna? Everyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.77,0:12:35.86,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,No objection.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.86,0:12:37.02,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,No objection.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.02,0:12:38.16,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,No objection.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.16,0:12:39.27,Default,Water Witch,0,0,0,,No objection.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.91,0:12:43.28,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,I will accept on one condition.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.14,0:12:45.28,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Which is?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.28,0:12:49.79,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,There is one member who is absent.\N The Wind Magician.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.12,0:12:52.41,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,Ah, the slacker.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.67,0:12:56.02,Flashback,Wind Magician,0,0,0,,Sorry, man. I'll let you\N handle it, Flamey.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.17,0:12:58.67,Flashback,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Come back here!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.67,0:13:01.26,Flashback,Wind Magician,0,0,0,,My bed is calling me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.29,0:13:06.68,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,He has designated me as his \Nproxy for all council votes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.04,0:13:10.53,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,You sure that wasn't meant \Nas a backhanded insult?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.53,0:13:12.83,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,You said it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.83,0:13:15.69,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,His vote will align with my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.69,0:13:17.69,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Huh? You can't do that!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.69,0:13:21.85,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Clearly, the Insect Magician \Nwill forfeit his own opinion
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.85,0:13:24.73,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,and just go with whatever \Nthe Beast Magician decides.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.73,0:13:28.83,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,If we are willing to allow that, then \Nmy request should not pose a problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.20,0:13:31.43,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.20,0:13:34.31,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Then let us all vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.90,0:13:46.22,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,All in favor, move to the right side.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.09,0:13:53.41,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Bird, Water, Beast, Insect. \NIn total, four votes in favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.18,0:13:57.23,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Now those opposed, move to the left side.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.20,0:14:04.61,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Flame, Fiore, Stone, and \NFlame's proxy vote for Wind.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.03,0:14:07.61,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,That is also four.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.12,0:14:15.41,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Hey. I've been wondering this whole time, \Nbut does she even know what we're saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.41,0:14:18.99,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,Yeah... I was sort of wondering myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.62,0:14:23.46,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,But then how do we make her understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.85,0:14:27.88,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Telepathically, she must have at \Nleast some grasp of the situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.21,0:14:30.26,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Does this mean you abstain?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.01,0:14:35.77,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.11,0:14:39.33,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,She started playing \Nwith some weird string.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.77,0:14:46.28,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Then with the Eastern Witch's abstention, \Nwe have a tie. Shall we vote again?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.08,0:14:52.26,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,Let's just get rid of Wind's vote. \NHe's absent so his vote should be invalid.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.26,0:14:53.48,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,What was that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.48,0:14:54.53,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,I wanna go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.92,0:14:57.67,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.24,0:15:06.24,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.24,0:15:11.80,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,The barrier should be preventing any \Noutsiders from infiltrating our meeting.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.04,0:15:17.43,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,Wait, Flame!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.07,0:15:33.57,Default,Stone Magician,0,0,0,,Isn't that...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.57,0:15:36.08,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,It's the Cat Witch after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.08,0:15:41.40,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,I heard she lost her life in the witch \Nhunts. Why is her spirit here?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.08,0:15:46.20,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,How could a spirit of the dead\N even penetrate the barrier?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.59,0:15:55.06,Italics,Cat Witch,0,0,0,,I believe in Luna.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.60,0:16:01.51,Italics,Cat Witch,0,0,0,,Luna. I believe... in her.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.51,0:16:03.59,Italics,Cat Witch,0,0,0,,I believe in her.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.50,0:16:14.42,Flashback_Italics,Dorothy,0,0,0,,Before, all the trees and animals of this \Nblack forest were contaminated with poison
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.42,0:16:16.99,Flashback_Italics,Dorothy,0,0,0,,and it was home to all sorts \Nof pests and evil spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.46,0:16:20.50,Flashback_Italics,Dorothy,0,0,0,,But once you moved here,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.50,0:16:23.85,Flashback_Italics,Dorothy,0,0,0,,it changed from a black forest \Nto a poison mushroom forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.85,0:16:26.47,Flashback_Italics,Dorothy,0,0,0,,I can feel safe letting \Nmy cats play here now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.65,0:16:33.31,Flashback_Italics,Dorothy,0,0,0,,Hey, it sounds kind of impersonal \Nwhen you call me "Miss Dorothy."
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.31,0:16:35.80,Flashback_Italics,Dorothy,0,0,0,,Just call me "Dorothy" \Nas if I was your sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.04,0:17:02.99,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,That puts the side in favor ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.89,0:17:07.14,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,In what way? That wasn't \Neven a council member,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.14,0:17:10.61,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,just a rude spirit that barged in \Nhere without having the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.06,0:17:12.74,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Counting that as a vote is absurd.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.74,0:17:14.05,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,Flame.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.30,0:17:18.30,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,That was a friend. \NThe tormented soul of a friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.30,0:17:20.81,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,Don't you think that's a little harsh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.81,0:17:22.22,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Crystal...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.00,0:17:30.82,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,She was willing to breach etiquette \Nin order to express her feelings.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.57,0:17:39.15,Flashback_Italics,Cat Witch,0,0,0,,I believe in Luna.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.83,0:17:45.27,Flashback_Italics,Cat Witch,0,0,0,,I believe in her.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.68,0:17:51.84,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Invalid!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.84,0:17:54.08,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,It is the one final wish and regret
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.08,0:17:56.44,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,preventing her spirit \Nfrom resting in peace,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.44,0:17:57.97,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,and you would flat-out reject it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.81,0:18:00.18,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,No changing the subject!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.10,0:18:03.54,Default,Beast Magician,0,0,0,,Baked potato.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.54,0:18:04.76,Default,Insect Magician,0,0,0,,Grilled cheese.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.54,0:18:15.38,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,The Cat Witch knew Luna quite well. She\N would not appear before us frivolously.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.38,0:18:18.20,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,In lieu of a proper requiem,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.20,0:18:21.62,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,why not allow this one \Nexception and grant her wish?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.59,0:18:25.12,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,Sounds good to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.62,0:18:26.67,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Flower?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.67,0:18:30.92,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,I just want to wrap things up. We aren't \Neven getting paid for being here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.92,0:18:32.63,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Is that what's bothering you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.63,0:18:34.46,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Let us set a deadline.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.13,0:18:39.88,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,None of us have any idea when that boy \Nmay transform into The End of All Things.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.88,0:18:45.83,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,But considering the amount of poison \Nthat Luna drew out of his body,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.83,0:18:50.82,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,he probably has at least three years. \NSo over the course of three years,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.82,0:18:55.09,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,if we conclude he shows no indication\N of having developed magical powers
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.09,0:18:57.25,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,strong enough to escape his destiny,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.90,0:18:59.78,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,we will sentence him to death.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.41,0:19:06.21,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Until that time, we members \Nof the Black Magician Council
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.53,0:19:13.57,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,will keep constant watch over you and the\N boy, and take turn making surprise visits
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.57,0:19:16.62,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,to present him with tests to complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.62,0:19:19.35,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,Huh? What a pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.35,0:19:20.47,Default,Crystal Witch,0,0,0,,Fiore...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.47,0:19:23.18,Default,Fiore Magician,0,0,0,,So will {\i1}that{\i0} be a paying job?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.65,0:19:27.68,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Flame. Are you willing \Nto wait three years?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.13,0:19:35.81,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,We don't know what the boy's intentions \Nare yet. What if he tries to escape?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.66,0:19:43.37,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,That will certainly require a response \Non our part. I already have
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.37,0:19:47.76,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,my familiar Claude currently serving \Nas eyes and ears for me here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.76,0:19:52.71,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Let us ask Claude to keep constant \Nwatch over both of them just in case.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.71,0:19:54.37,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,Is that all right, Claude?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.37,0:19:56.33,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Yes, Master Bird.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.41,0:19:59.71,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,All right with you, Luna?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.96,0:20:01.77,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Y-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.22,0:20:07.92,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,As the boy's master, I will let you \Ndecide how much to tell him about this,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.92,0:20:10.75,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,but please make your \Ndecision very carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.69,0:20:17.29,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Any time in those three years, \Nif that boy cannot pass our trials,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.82,0:20:22.65,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,tries to run away, or shows any sign \Nof becoming The End of All Things,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.65,0:20:26.53,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,I will not hesitate.\N I will come to kill him myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.38,0:20:29.16,Default,Flame Magician,0,0,0,,Bear this in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.85,0:20:33.92,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.92,0:20:39.96,Default,Bird Magician,0,0,0,,And with that, the Black Witch \NCouncil is now adjourned.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.93,0:20:44.93,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.93,0:20:46.93,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Wow!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.21,0:20:48.93,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.25,0:20:53.19,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Why? Did they really have\Nto blast us with wind?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.88,0:20:55.35,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Or are they just harassing us?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.34,0:21:00.66,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Anyway, things are gonna \Nget crazy for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.19,0:21:06.20,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,You really up to this, Luna? Well, you \Nsure stood your ground back there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.42,0:21:07.43,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Luna?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.43,0:21:10.34,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Hey, is that boy gonna \Nbe in our family now?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.68,0:21:15.21,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,We've never had a human in our \Nfamily before. Have we, Luna?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.21,0:21:17.23,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Luna? Oops!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.71,0:21:19.56,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Luna's asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.93,0:21:23.61,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.70,0:21:28.69,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.69,0:21:32.46,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,You've gotta be kidding me! How can \Nyou fall asleep after all that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.46,0:21:36.44,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,She's just tired after being surrounded \Nby all those scary people!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.44,0:21:40.03,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,She had to fix the house and \Nuse all kinds of magic, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.03,0:21:44.52,Default,Claude,0,0,0,,Yeah? Well I'm tired, too! Wake up! \NI said wake the hell up, damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.89,0:21:44.52,Default - Top,Minos,0,0,0,,Please keep your voice down!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.02,0:21:49.49,Flashback_Italics,Cat Witch,0,0,0,,I believe in Luna. I believe in her.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.74,0:21:58.44,Italics,Narr,0,0,0,,The witch said that she \Nhad a dream that night.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.40,0:22:04.23,Italics,Narr,0,0,0,,I was not able to ask her \Nexactly what it was about,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.82,0:22:12.34,Italics,Narr,0,0,0,,but Luna, I pray that your \Ndreams are always joyful.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.14,0:22:16.84,Italics,Narr,0,0,0,,I still pray for that \Ntoday, just as I did then.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.98,0:22:23.74,Italics,Narr,0,0,0,,And so this is how I and Luna, \Na witch who could touch no one,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.21,0:22:28.25,Italics,Narr,0,0,0,,began our hectic but always \Nwondrous life together,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.25,0:22:30.99,Italics,Narr,0,0,0,,in a home overflowing \Nwith magic and mushrooms.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.04,0:22:38.17,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,TRANSLATION: MICHAEL ARNOLD
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.33,0:22:41.42,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,SUBTITLE TIMING: ANDY ELLIS\NEDITING: ELISABETH CRIST
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.75,0:22:46.13,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,QUALITY CHECK: GABRIELLA ALABANZA\NTRANSLATION CHECK: MICHELLE TYMON
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.61,0:24:10.25,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,NEXT TIME:\N I CANNOT RETURN TO THE CAT FOREST
